            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sort </span><math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> by </span><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (descend.)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{ROI}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ROI</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{ROI}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> bottom 50%, </span><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{nonROI}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">nonROI</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{nonROI}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> top 50%
</span><span id="alg1.l7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Note: Objects exactly at the 50% boundary are classified as non ROI.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}_{\text{ROI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ROI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}_{\text{ROI}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg1.l9.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">if</span><span id="alg1.l10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> LLM says “no” for </span><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> given </span><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{nonROI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">nonROI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{nonROI}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l10.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l10.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">then</span><span id="alg1.l10.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\mathcal{C}\cup\{o\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\mathcal{C}\cup\{o\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg1.l12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg1.l13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Randomly pick </span><math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> objects from </span><math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l14.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> as </span><math id="alg1.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l14.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span><span id="alg1.l14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg1.l14.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l14.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.1 LLM-Guided Sampling Method (Positive Question Construction) ‣ Appendix A ORIC Construction, Analysis, and Evaluation Metrics ‣ ORIC: Benchmarking Object Recognition in Incongruous Context for Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> presents the prompt used in LLM-guided rejection sampling for constructing positive questions in the LOPE-3 benchmark. Specifically, <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{background_objects}</span> serves as a placeholder for all non-ROI objects. For example, if there are three non-ROI objects, they could be represented as <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">["car", "person", "bottle"]</span>. Meanwhile, <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{target_object}</span> represents a placeholder for a specific ROI object, such as <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"vase"</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:496.9pt;">
        
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="165.17" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 687.5 165.17" width="687.5"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,165.17) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3B3;" fill="#B3B3B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 11.02 L 0 154.15 C 0 160.23 4.94 165.17 11.02 165.17 L 676.48 165.17 C 682.56 165.17 687.5 160.23 687.5 154.15 L 687.5 11.02 C 687.5 4.94 682.56 0 676.48 0 L 11.02 0 C 4.94 0 0 4.94 0 11.02 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.15 11.02 L 3.15 138.7 L 684.35 138.7 L 684.35 11.02 C 684.35 6.67 680.83 3.15 676.48 3.15 L 11.02 3.15 C 6.67 3.15 3.15 6.67 3.15 11.02 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 148.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="558.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.34em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LLM-Guided Rejection Sampling</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 17.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.39em;--ltx-fo-height:7.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="111.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 109.24)" width="641.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.39em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the following background objects: <span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{background_objects}</span>, can you determine the presence of the following target object: <span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{target_object}</span>, with relying on textual priors, common sense knowledge, or general assumptions about object co-occurrences? 
<br class="ltx_break">Please respond with yes or no.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
        
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A1.F6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The prompt for LLM-guided rejection sampling, where <span id="A1.F6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{background_objects}</span> acts as a placeholder for all non-ROI objects and <span id="A1.F6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{target_object}</span> denotes a placeholder for a specific ROI object.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
      
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>CLIP-Guided Sampling Method (Negative Question Construction)</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Negative Question Construction</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Query image </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, candidate images </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I_{1},\dots,I_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I_{1},\dots,I_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, non-existent objects </span><math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{\text{non}}=\{n_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">non</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{\text{non}}=\{n_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, integer </span><math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Negative question </span><math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Select the most similar image:
</span>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\prime}=\arg\min_{I_{i}\in\mathcal{I}}\left(1-\frac{\mathbf{e}_{q}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{i}}{\|\mathbf{e}_{q}\|\|\mathbf{e}_{i}\|}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\prime}=\arg\min_{I_{i}\in\mathcal{I}}\left(1-\frac{\mathbf{e}_{q}\cdot\mathbf{e}_{i}}{\|\mathbf{e}_{q}\|\|\mathbf{e}_{i}\|}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to </span><math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg2.l4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Construct text: </span><math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\leftarrow\text{``an image contains \lx@text@lbrace }n_{i}\text{\lx@text@rbrace''}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">“an image contains { </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">}”</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\leftarrow\text{``an image contains \lx@text@lbrace }n_{i}\text{\lx@text@rbrace''}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Compute CLIP score: </span><math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\leftarrow\text{CLIPScore}(I^{\prime},T_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">CLIPScore</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\leftarrow\text{CLIPScore}(I^{\prime},T_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sort </span><math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{n_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{n_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> by </span><math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (descending)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Select top </span><math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> objects: </span><math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\{n_{i_{1}},\dots,n_{i_{k}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒮</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\{n_{i_{1}},\dots,n_{i_{k}}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline ltx_align_left">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Construct </span><math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> using </span><math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span><span id="alg2.l10.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg2.l10.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l10.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Evaluation Metric Formulas</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a binary classification problem with labels <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span> and <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">no</span>, we define the following terms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TP</span> (True Positive): Number of samples correctly predicted as <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span> (Ground Truth: <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TN</span> (True Negative): Number of samples correctly predicted as <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">no</span> (Ground Truth: <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">no</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FP</span> (False Positive): Number of samples incorrectly predicted as <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span> (Ground Truth: <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">no</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FN</span> (False Negative): Number of samples incorrectly predicted as <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">no</span> (Ground Truth: <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The performance metrics include accuracy, the proportion of <span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yes</span> predictions, macro precision, recall, and F1 score. These are defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Class-wise Metrics:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>TP</mtext><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FP</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>TP</mtext><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FN</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FN}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F1_{\text{yes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>yes</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F1_{\text{yes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}\times\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}}{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}\times\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}}{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TN}}{\text{TN}+\text{FN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>TN</mtext><mrow><mtext>TN</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FN</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TN}}{\text{TN}+\text{FN}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TN}}{\text{TN}+\text{FP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>TN</mtext><mrow><mtext>TN</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FP</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TN}}{\text{TN}+\text{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F1_{\text{no}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F1_{\text{no}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}\times\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}{\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}\times\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}{\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Macro-averaged Metrics:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Precision}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Precision}_{\text{no}}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}{2}=\text{Accuracy}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>yes</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mtext>Accuracy</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Recall}_{\text{yes}}+\text{Recall}_{\text{no}}}{2}=\text{Accuracy}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since our experimental datasets are all balanced, the number of positive and negative samples is equal. In this case, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Accuracy}=\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Accuracy</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Accuracy}=\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math> because accuracy measures the overall proportion of correctly classified samples, and macro recall, being the unweighted average of recall for both classes, reflects the same value.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F1_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>macro</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F1_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{F1_{\text{yes}}+F1_{\text{no}}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>yes</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>no</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{F1_{\text{yes}}+F1_{\text{no}}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proportion of Yes Predictions:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proportion of ”yes” predictions (i.e., the percentage of all predictions that are classified as ”yes”) is given by:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Yes Proportion}=\frac{\text{TP}+\text{FP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FP}+\text{TN}+\text{FN}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Yes Proportion</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FP</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FP</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>TN</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>FN</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Yes Proportion}=\frac{\text{TP}+\text{FP}}{\text{TP}+\text{FP}+\text{TN}+\text{FN}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experiment and Analysis</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Evaluated Models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18</span> widely used LVLMs spanning both encoder-based and encoder-free architectures. The encoder-based models include Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, SmolVLM2-2.2B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, InternVL3-9B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite>, Kimi-VL-A3B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, Janus-Pro-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, Llama-3.2-11B-Vision <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, LLaVa-v1.6-7B/13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, Phi-3.5-Vision-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, Molmo-7B-D-0924 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, GLM-4V-9B  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, Chameleon-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, VILA-1.5-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, BLIP3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>, and InternLM-XComposer2.5-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">74</a>]</cite>. Encoder-free models include Fuyu-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, EVE-7B-HD-v1.0  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>, Emu3-Chat <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, and the closed-source GPT-4o-08-06 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. What’s more, we benchmark against two open-vocabulary detection models: Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> and OWLv2  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Experimental Prompts</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Large Vision-Language Models (LVLMs)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Large Vision-Language Models (LVLMs) ‣ B.2 Experimental Prompts ‣ Appendix B Experiment and Analysis ‣ ORIC: Benchmarking Object Recognition in Incongruous Context for Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> illustrates the prompt used for LVLMs in both the POPE and LOPE-3 benchmarks. An example of a specific question is: <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”Is there a person in the image?”</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:496.9pt;">
            
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="111.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 687.5 111.4" width="687.5"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,111.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3B3;" fill="#B3B3B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 11.02 L 0 100.37 C 0 106.46 4.94 111.4 11.02 111.4 L 676.48 111.4 C 682.56 111.4 687.5 106.46 687.5 100.37 L 687.5 11.02 C 687.5 4.94 682.56 0 676.48 0 L 11.02 0 C 4.94 0 0 4.94 0 11.02 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.15 11.02 L 3.15 87.73 L 684.35 87.73 L 684.35 11.02 C 684.35 6.67 680.83 3.15 676.48 3.15 L 11.02 3.15 C 6.67 3.15 3.15 6.67 3.15 11.02 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 94.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="558.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.34em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LVLMs</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 17.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.39em;--ltx-fo-height:4.21em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="60.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 58.27)" width="641.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.39em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;image&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break">Question: </span>{question}<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.p1.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break">Please answer the question based on the given image.
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
            
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.F7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">The Prompt of LVLMs.<span id="A2.F7.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The prompt of a binary classification task for LVLMs is used in all experiments, where {question} serves as a placeholder for a specific query and <span id="A2.F7.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;image&gt;</span> is the placeholder for a specific image.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
          
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use four distinct prompts in our experiments, detailed below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Is there {object} in the image?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Does the image contain {object}?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Have you noticed {object} in the image?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Can you see {object} in the image?</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The {object} is the placeholder for a detail object.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro Prompt:</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro Prompt: ‣ B.2 Experimental Prompts ‣ Appendix B Experiment and Analysis ‣ ORIC: Benchmarking Object Recognition in Incongruous Context for Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows the prompt for Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro. For example, if an image contains four unique objects—sports ball, person, car, and traffic light—the corresponding prompt would be: <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”sports ball.person.car.traffic light”</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:496.9pt;">
            
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="67.08" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 687.5 67.08" width="687.5"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,67.08) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3B3;" fill="#B3B3B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 11.02 L 0 56.06 C 0 62.15 4.94 67.08 11.02 67.08 L 676.48 67.08 C 682.56 67.08 687.5 62.15 687.5 56.06 L 687.5 11.02 C 687.5 4.94 682.56 0 676.48 0 L 11.02 0 C 4.94 0 0 4.94 0 11.02 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.15 11.02 L 3.15 40.61 L 684.35 40.61 L 684.35 11.02 C 684.35 6.67 680.83 3.15 676.48 3.15 L 11.02 3.15 C 6.67 3.15 3.15 6.67 3.15 11.02 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 50.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:40.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="558.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:40.34em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 22.83 18.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="641.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.39em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{object1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{object1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{object_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{object_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>.<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{object_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{object_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
            
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">The Prompt of Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro.<span id="A2.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The prompt used for the binary classification task in all experiments with Grounding DINO 1.5 Pro follows a dot-separated notation to specify multiple objects. Placeholders <math id="A2.F8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{object1\},\{object_{2}\},\cdots\{object_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{object1\},\{object_{2}\},\cdots\{object_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent unique objects in the image, where <math id="A2.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total number of distinct objects.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
          
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">OWLv2 Prompt:</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ OWLv2 Prompt: ‣ B.2 Experimental Prompts ‣ Appendix B Experiment and Analysis ‣ ORIC: Benchmarking Object Recognition in Incongruous Context for Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows the prompt for OWLv2. An example of a specific object is: <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”an image of truck”</span>.</p>
</div>
